Note: The abbreviations used in the table are as follows:
2D/3D T1w MRI – two-/three-dimensional T1-weighted magnetic resonance imaging;
AD – Alzheimer’s disease;
Acc – accuracy;
AUC – area under the receiver operating characteristic curve; β \beta -VAE – beta variational autoencoder;
CAE – convolutional autoencoder;
CN – cognitively normal;
CNN – convolutional neural network;
EMCI – early mild cognitive impairment;
LBP – local binary patterns;
LMCI – late mild cognitive impairment;
mAP – mean average precision;
mRMR – minimum redundancy maximum relevance feature selection;
PCA – principal component analysis;
PLS-DA – partial least squares discriminant analysis;
SE-ADA – style encoder adversarial domain adaptation;
SMCI – stable mild cognitive impairment.

